    Copyright (c) 2020, Braille Institute of America, Inc.
    Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
    https://www.brailleinstitute.org/freefont

    Files: app/ui/src/assets/fonts/AtkinsonHyperlegible-Regular.woff2
           app/ui/src/assets/fonts/AtkinsonHyperlegible-Bold.woff2
    Licence text: app/ui/src/assets/fonts/OFL.txt (the full OFL 1.1, as
           published by SIL, with the typeface's own copyright line)

    The typeface was chosen for the reason it exists: its letterforms are
    distinguished from each other rather than from a style, which is what makes
    b/d, I/l/1 and 0/O separable for a reader who is guessing. It is the one
    third-party asset in this repository.

    The full OFL 1.1 text accompanies these files in the same directory, and
    `bundle-corpus.mjs` is not what carries it — the fonts are bundled by the
    renderer build, and the licence sits beside them so it cannot be separated
    from what it licenses.

